  "lineage": "Music of the Bamileke chiefdoms of the western Grassfields, played at the chief's compound and above all at funerals, when the chiefdom's societies perform song and dance with drums, bells and rattles. Bernard Surugue recorded the funeral of a Bamileke queen in 1974 for a SELAF/ORSTOM LP. Generic drum, double-bell and shaker cards stand in for the instruments.",
